<% layout("/layouts/boilerplate") %>

<div class="container-xl">
  <article class="legal">
    <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-muted">Last updated: <%= lastUpdated %></p>
    <p>
      Travel Roots ("Travel Roots", "we", "us") lets guests discover and book stays offered by hosts. This policy
      explains what personal information we collect, why we collect it, who we share it with and the choices you
      have. It applies to the Travel Roots website and related services.
    </p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#collect">Information we collect</a></li>
        <li><a href="#use">How we use information</a></li>
        <li><a href="#bases">Legal bases</a></li>
        <li><a href="#share">Who we share it with</a></li>
        <li><a href="#transfers">International transfers</a></li>
        <li><a href="#retention">How long we keep it</a></li>
        <li><a href="#rights">Your rights and choices</a></li>
        <li><a href="#security">Security</a></li>
        <li><a href="#children">Children</a></li>
        <li><a href="#changes">Changes and contact</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <h2 id="collect">1. Information we collect</h2>
    <p><strong>Information you give us</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Account details:</strong> username, email address and password. Passwords are stored only as a salted PBKDF2 hash and are never visible to us.</li>
      <li><strong>Profile details:</strong> optional display name, phone number, location and a short bio.</li>
      <li><strong>Listings:</strong> title, description, photos, location, nightly price and the contact phone number and email you provide for guests.</li>
      <li><strong>Bookings:</strong> the stay you book, your dates, the amounts charged and the order and payment references returned by our payment provider.</li>
      <li><strong>Reviews and saved stays:</strong> ratings, review text and the stays you add to your wishlist.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Information from third parties</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>If you sign in with <strong>Google</strong> or <strong>GitHub</strong>, we receive your provider ID, name, email address and profile photo.</li>
      <li><strong>Razorpay</strong> tells us whether a payment succeeded. We never receive or store your card, UPI or bank details.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Information collected automatically</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Technical data such as your IP address, browser type and the pages you request, recorded in server logs and used for security and rate limiting.</li>
      <li>Cookies and local storage as described in our <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="use">2. How we use information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To create and manage your account and let you sign in.</li>
      <li>To publish listings, show reviews and run search.</li>
      <li>To process bookings and payments, and to show receipts to guests and reservations to hosts.</li>
      <li>To keep the service secure, for example by limiting repeated sign-in attempts and verifying payments.</li>
      <li>To send service messages such as password reset emails. We do not send marketing emails.</li>
      <li>To comply with legal, tax and accounting obligations.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="bases">3. Legal bases</h2>
    <p>
      Where data protection laws such as India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 or the EU General Data
      Protection Regulation apply, we process your information because it is necessary to provide the service you
      asked for, because we have a legitimate interest in keeping the service secure and working well, because the
      law requires it, or because you have given consent (for example, to preference storage). You can withdraw
      consent at any time.
    </p>

    <h2 id="share">4. Who we share it with</h2>
    <p>We do not sell your personal information. We share it only as needed to run Travel Roots:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Other users:</strong> your display name, photo and reviews are public. Hosts see the name of guests who book with them. Guests see the contact details a host adds to a listing.</li>
      <li><strong>Razorpay</strong> processes payments.</li>
      <li><strong>Cloudinary</strong> stores and delivers listing photos.</li>
      <li><strong>MongoDB Atlas</strong> hosts our database and <strong>Render</strong> hosts the application.</li>
      <li><strong>Geoapify</strong> converts a listing's location text into map coordinates. Only the location text is sent.</li>
      <li><strong>Google</strong> and <strong>GitHub</strong>, if you choose to sign in with them.</li>
      <li><strong>Email providers</strong> deliver password reset messages.</li>
      <li><strong>Authorities</strong>, when we are legally required to, or to protect the rights and safety of our users.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="transfers">5. International transfers</h2>
    <p>
      Our service providers may store or process information outside your country. When that happens we rely on
      the safeguards these providers offer and on applicable law to protect your information.
    </p>

    <h2 id="retention">6. How long we keep it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Account, profile, listing and review data are kept until you delete them or delete your account.</li>
      <li>Records of completed payments are retained for as long as tax and accounting laws require, even after an account is deleted, but are no longer linked to a profile.</li>
      <li>Sessions expire 7 days after your last visit. Password reset links expire after one hour.</li>
      <li>Server logs are kept for a limited period for security and troubleshooting.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="rights">7. Your rights and choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Access and correction:</strong> view and update your details in <a href="/profile/settings">Account settings</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Deletion:</strong> delete your account at any time from Account settings. Listings, reviews and saved stays are removed immediately.</li>
      <li><strong>Consent:</strong> change your cookie choices with the "Cookie settings" link in the footer.</li>
      <li><strong>Other requests:</strong> to request a copy of your data, raise a concern or appoint a nominee, email us. You may also complain to your local data protection authority.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="security">8. Security</h2>
    <p>
      We use HTTPS, hashed passwords, secure HttpOnly session cookies, protection against cross-site request
      forgery, strict content security headers, rate limiting and server-side payment verification. No system is
      completely secure, so please use a strong, unique password and tell us if you notice anything suspicious.
    </p>

    <h2 id="children">9. Children</h2>
    <p>
      Travel Roots is intended for people aged 18 and over. We do not knowingly collect information from children.
      If you believe a child has created an account, contact us and we will remove it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes">10. Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>
      We will update this policy when our practices change and revise the date at the top. For any privacy question
      or request, contact <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</div>
